he function, applying the addition, constant multiple, and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+24x-7) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{x}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3{x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(24x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-7) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})-3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+24\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-7\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =-3{x}^{(3-1)}-3\\cdot 2{x}^{(2-1)}+24\\cdot 1-7\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-3{x}^{2}-6x+24\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316988 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316989 13194139534879 true] [17592186316988 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534879 true] [17592186316988 1041 "field-1" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316988 1104 #edb/ref 17592186316989 13194139534879 true] [17592186316988 1110 #uuid "4326c645-1ad3-5aed-8f60-91004839b56b" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316989 1034 "-3x^2-6x+24" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316989 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534879 true] [17592186316989 1111 #uuid "9e91d8c0-34da-51b2-b77b-8ac14c502e44" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316990 1017 #edb/ref 17592186316991 13194139534879 true] [17592186316990 1089 "q-128283" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316990 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534879 true] [17592186316990 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=-{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+24x-7.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nCalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(x)\\,=\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3x^2-6x+24$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nIf $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2}$ are the critical points of $f(x),$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\,=\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316990 1113 #uuid "ab2fd3ad-2935-5251-acc3-c0f04970e089" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316990 1145 "A critical point of $f(x)$ is a point $x=c$ in the domain of $f$ such that either ${f}^{′}(c)=0$ or ${f}^{′}(c)$ does not exist.\n\nPreviously, we found that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-3{x}^{2}-6x+24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to find the critical points:\n\n* First, we compute the points where ${f}^{′}(c)=0.$ We set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}^{2}-6x+24 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x-8 & =0 \\\\ (x+4)(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-4,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has stationary points at $x=-4$ and $x=2.$ \n\n* Second, we note that ${f}^{′}(x)$ exists for all values of $x$ in the domain of $f(x).$ So $f(x)$ has no non-stationary critical points.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the critical points of $f(x)$ are $x={x}_{1}=-4$ and $x={x}_{2}=2.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=-4\\cdot 2=-8.\n$$" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316991 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316992 13194139534879 true] [17592186316991 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534879 true] [17592186316991 1041 "field-1" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316991 1104 #edb/ref 17592186316992 13194139534879 true] [17592186316991 1110 #uuid "985dcd21-b215-519c-80c9-77d60646aaae" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316992 1034 "-8" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316992 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534879 true] [17592186316992 1111 #uuid "64b48d89-f704-50a0-b695-a0d1df18cae4" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316993 1017 #edb/ref 17592186316994 13194139534879 true] [17592186316993 1017 #edb/ref 17592186316996 13194139534879 true] [17592186316993 1089 "q-128284" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316993 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534879 true] [17592186316993 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=-{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+24x-7.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nCalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(x)\\,=\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3x^2-6x+24$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nIf $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2}$ are the critical points of $f(x),$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$\n\n                            \n           