\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,)$" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316993 1113 #uuid "4bec7a07-28c1-5fb2-9ffa-37e07c5a537a" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316993 1145 "The function is increasing where ${f}^{′}(x)>0.$ \n\nPreviously, we found that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=-3{x}^{2}-6x+24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to solve the inequality\n\n$$\n-3{x}^{2}-6x+24>0.\n$$\n\nThe above inequality factors as\n\n$$\n-3(x+4)(x-2)>0.\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=-3(x+4)(x-2)$ has roots at $x=-4$ and $x=2,$ as shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042687/assets/41fbc51820e147872fddfd0f124f0235a26513992f07a4b5681f2d8cb25d4a3b.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the function is increasing for $x\\in (-4,2).$" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316995 13194139534879 true] [17592186316994 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534879 true] [17592186316994 1041 "field-1" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316994 1104 #edb/ref 17592186316995 13194139534879 true] [17592186316994 1110 #uuid "8d1250b7-66d6-5af7-83c7-c9546a0af4a5" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316995 1034 "-4" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316995 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534879 true] [17592186316995 1111 #uuid "0087ccd5-dcb0-5d7b-8820-be57e0c99862" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316997 13194139534879 true] [17592186316996 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534879 true] [17592186316996 1041 "field-2" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316996 1104 #edb/ref 17592186316997 13194139534879 true] [17592186316996 1110 #uuid "b2006850-9c49-5299-ae93-b099ef7d5a37" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316997 1034 "2" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316997 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534879 true] [17592186316997 1111 #uuid "fd3f7411-25a8-5305-af02-9