                                        $-8$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the values of $x$ for which the function $f(x)$ is increasing.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $f(x)$ is increasing for $x\\,\\in \\,($ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,,\\,$  \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,)$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFor which values of $x$ does the function $f(x)$ have local maxima and local minima?\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$  \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \nis a local minimum\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$  \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \nis a local maximum" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316998 1113 #uuid "39a0f9d2-488f-5ef5-9f41-ec3876e3f6f9" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316998 1145 "We have the derivative \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-3{x}^{2}-6x+24=-3(x+4)(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the two critical points $x=-4$ and $x=2.$ We use the first derivative test to determine whether these points are local maxima or minima.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-5,0,3$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-5) & =-3(-5+4)(-5-2)=-21<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & =-3(0+4)(0-2)=24>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & =-3(3+4)(3-2)=-21<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in the table shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,-4)$ | $-4$ | $(-4,2)$ | $2$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-5$ |  | $0$ |  | $3$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ |\n| $f$ | $↘$ | min | $↗$ | max | $↘$ |\n\n \nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical points.\n\n* At $x=-4,$ the first derivative changes sign from negative to positive. Therefore, $x=-4$ is a local minimum.\n\n* At $x=2,$ the first derivative changes sign from positive to negative. Therefore, $x=2$ is a local maximum." 13194139534879 true] [17592186316999 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317000 13194139534879 true] [17592186316999 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534879 true] [17592186316999 1041 "field-1" 13194139534879 true] [17592186316999 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317000 13194139534879 true] [17592186316999 1110 #uuid "647a8609-7527-55b9-b2cd-71b632319a41" 13194139534879 true] [17592186317000 1034 "-4" 13194139534879 true] [17592186317000 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534879 true] [17592186317000 1111 #uuid "ba381183-3e3b-51d3-be77-cd6419b2a4b9" 13194139534879 true] [17592186317001 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317002 13194139534879 true] [17592186317001 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534879 true] [17592186317001 1041 "field-2" 13194139534879 true] [17592186317001 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317002 13194139534879 true] [17592186317001 1110 #uuid "f9c92eb8-a333-5cc2-8ca9-dc5a92bb494f" 13194139534879 true] [17592186317002 1034 "2" 13194139534879 true] [17592186317002 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534879 true] [17592186317002 1111 #uuid "a62b386b-c4c9-5058-a7ce-e9e9f1ff1d14" 13194139534879 true] [17592186317003 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317004 13194139534879 