which the function $f(x)$ is increasing.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $f(x)$ is increasing for $x\\,\\in \\,($ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,,\\,$  \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,)$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nFor which values of $x$ does the function $f(x)$ have local maxima and local minima?\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$  \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \nis a local minimum\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$  \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \nis a local maximum\n\nCurrent part:\n\nWhat are the global maximum and global minimum values of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-1,3]?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The global maximum is ${f}_{max}\\,=\\,$  \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The global minimum is ${f}_{min}\\,=\\,$  \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}" 13194139534879 true] [17592186317003 1113 #uuid "6bbdc17e-2e75-51ae-9305-829559459a78" 13194139534879 true] [17592186317003 1145 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We already know the critical points of the function:\n\n$$\nx=-4,\\,x=2.\n$$\n\nSince $x=-4$ does not belong to the interval $[-1,3]$, the critical points on the interval $[-1,3]$ are $x=2,$ and the endpoints $x=-1$ and $x=3$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =-(-1)^{3}-3(-1)^{2}+24(-1)-7=-33 \\\\ f(2) & =-(2)^{3}-3(2)^{2}+24(2)-7=21 \\\\ f(3) & =-(3)^{3}-3(3)^{2}+24(3)-7=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step 2.\n\n* The great